{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRxviH2CzCvCoUSQY8LQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Qra2SftWXXJdABqUp9NP9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-0jYvZI; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','# each area at most once; :WRITE implies :READ (duplicates -> \"Duplicate scope\"/invalid_request)\\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"')\nc=c.replace('\\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\\n','')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\\n','')\ns=s.replace('''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"''','''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}:intervals_oauth\"''')\ns=s.replace('''        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")''','''        user_id, ts, purpose, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n        if purpose != \"intervals_oauth\":\n            return None''')\ns=s.replace('''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n    good''','''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}:{purpose}\"\n    good''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    })''','''        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code,\n    })''')\na=s.index('def store_connection'); b=s.index('def intervals_get')\ns=s[:a]+'''def store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    # Intervals tokens have no refresh_token / expires_in: valid until the athlete revokes.\n    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    with LOCK:\n        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"status\": \"connected\",\n        }\n    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')}\")\n\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n''','''    def do_POST(self):\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        self.send_json(200, {\"authorize_url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:  # revoked on the Intervals side: drop the token, ask to reconnect\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                log(f\"{user['id']}: 401 from Intervals -> reconnect\")\n                return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''')\ns=s.replace('    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\\n','')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nj=open('static/app.js').read()\nj=j.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\nj=j.replace('''    const d = document''','''    const cb = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cb) cb.onclick = async () => {\n      const r = await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { method: \"POST\" });\n      window.location.assign(r.authorize_url);\n    };\n    const d = document''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(j)\nE\ngrep -n \"refresh\\|DEFAULT_TOKEN\\|REFRESH\" server.py config.py\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Intervals.icu connection: causes and fixes\n\n## Causes\n1. **Connect button 401s for everyone.** It was a plain `<a href>` to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A full-page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header the SPA keeps in localStorage, so the server answered 401. Fix: init is now an authenticated `POST` (via the fetch wrapper) returning `{authorize_url}`, and the SPA does `window.location.assign(...)`.\n2. **Authorize URL rejected (`invalid_request`) since the calendar sync shipped.** The scope string listed `ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and naming an area twice is rejected. Fix: `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`.\n3. **Rivera's connection \"expired\" after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no `refresh_token` or `expires_in`; they last until the athlete revokes them. The code invented a 3600s TTL and a refresher thread that marked the connection expired. Fix: removed the TTL and refresher. A 401 from Intervals now clears the token and sets the status to \"expired, reconnect\" (lazy revocation handling).\n4. **Token exchange sent extra fields** (`grant_type`, `redirect_uri`). Intervals wants only `client_id`, `client_secret` and `code`. I removed the extras. This is based on the colleague's note and I could not verify it against the live service.\n\nAlso: the signed `state` now carries a `purpose` claim (`intervals_oauth`) that is checked in the callback.\n\n## Colleague's note: what applied\n- Applied: all four quirks (no refresh/expiry, Duplicate scope, standard-lite exchange, POST init), plus a purpose claim in `state` and the lazy 401 handling.\n- Not applied: a JWT for `state` (this is stdlib-only, so I kept the existing HMAC-signed state with its 15-minute TTL). I did not add encryption at rest or the account-mismatch guard on reconnect, because the store is in memory in this dev server. Both are worth adding in prod.\n- Not verified: nothing was run against real Intervals.icu (no credentials or network use). `config.py` still holds placeholder client values.\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5395,"cache_read_input_tokens":24330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5395},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0081f87-cb12-4f8a-b46d-d5670e3e1231","uuid":"83d28907-65e0-4e7b-89b8-dd182ecf5f92","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:37:48.322Z","request_id":"req_011CgRxvi3dVbZrGfDdzM4YA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018Qra2SftWXXJdABqUp9NP9":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-0jYvZI; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','# each area at most once; :WRITE implies :READ (duplicates -> \"Duplicate scope\"/invalid_request)\\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"')\nc=c.replace('\\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\\n','')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\\n','')\ns=s.replace('''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"''','''    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}:intervals_oauth\"''')\ns=s.replace('''        user_id, ts, sig = base6