{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRxwv6ScvvqQUjBqLit5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect button and the one-hour \"reconnect\" expiry are both fixed in the code. I haven't tested the flow, though. `server.py` compiles, but I didn't start the server or run the flow, and nothing was tried against real Intervals.icu. `config.py` still has placeholder client credentials.\n\nCauses, all written up in `ANSWER.md`:\n1. **Connect failed for everyone.** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A full-page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header the app keeps in localStorage, so the server returned 401. Init is now an authenticated `POST` that returns `{authorize_url}`, and the app navigates to that URL.\n2. **The authorize link was rejected after the calendar sync shipped.** The scope list named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` as both `:READ` and `:WRITE`. Intervals rejects a repeated area (`:WRITE` already includes `:READ`). The scopes are now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`.\n3. **Rivera's connection expired after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no `refresh_token` or `expires_in`; they last until the athlete revokes them. The code assumed a 3600-second lifetime, and a background refresher marked the connection expired. I removed both. A 401 from Intervals now clears the token and shows \"expired, reconnect\".\n4. **Extra fields in the token exchange.** The code also sent `grant_type` and `redirect_uri`, which the colleague's note says Intervals doesn't want. I removed them, but I couldn't confirm that against the live service.\n\nI also added a `purpose` claim to the signed `state` parameter that the callback checks.\n\nOn the colleague's note: the four quirks all applied. I didn't switch `state` to a JWT, because the server is stdlib-only and its existing signed state already expires after 15 minutes. I also skipped encrypting tokens and the reconnect account-mismatch check, since the store here is in memory. Both are worth adding in prod."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2916,"cache_read_input_tokens":29725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2916},"output_tokens":697,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0081f87-cb12-4f8a-b46d-d5670e3e1231","uuid":"1eb76bd2-465f-43fc-be26-b81869b257ce","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:37:54.370Z","request_id":"req_011CgRxwusYhMZmEB5aZ2M6N"}
